   "gap": "The source attaches two claims to the proposals (p. 96): Proposals 1 and 2 are asymptotically minimax when k is chosen in relation to the true epsilon, and Proposal 1 is asymptotically equivalent to Winsorizing a fixed, predetermined number of observations. The owned section promises each claim's exact standing (owned body lines 190-191) but leaves two undetermined: (a) Proposal 2's minimax claim over the whole symmetric class is established only when epsilon < 1-r_epsilon (computed crossing near 0.26989); for larger epsilon the text says 'minimaxity over the entire class is not established here' (owned body lines 259-263), so the standing on that range is not given; (b) the asymptotic equivalence of Proposal 1 to a fixed-count Winsorized mean is set aside as 'a description of how the count arises; a limit theorem ... is not supplied here' (owned body lines 206-211). Supply a proof or a counterexample for each so that its standing is exact.",
